  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `camcraft-geometry` gets `sketch_recipe::SketchRecipe`. It has four shapes: rectangle (optional corner radius), circle, obround and regular polygon (across flats or across corners).\n- A recipe compiles to exact `Line`, `Arc` and `Circle` primitives in a `SketchData`. The outline is closed, counterclockwise and centred on the profile origin, on the layer `outline`.\n- A bad dimension is refused by name and never clamped. The refusals are: not finite, below 0.1 mm, above 100000 mm, a negative corner radius, a corner radius larger than half the smaller side, an obround wider than long, fewer than 3 or more than 1000 sides, and a straight edge shorter than 0.1 mm.\n- `Sketch` gets `recipe: Option<SketchRecipe>`. `SketchDto` stores it as `recipe`. `PROJECT_VERSION` goes from 84 to 85.\n- On load, the stored recipe is compiled again. If it does not give the stored outline bit for bit, the file is refused by the profile's name.\n- New undoable commands: `CreateSketchRecipe`, `EditSketchRecipe` and `AddQuickOp`. `AddQuickOp` is one `BatchCommand`: the recipe profile and a 2D Contour on it. One undo removes the two.\n- `EditSketchRecipe` writes the new outline. The operations on the profile go stale through their existing stamp.\n- New MCP tools in `crates/app/src/mcp/sketch_recipe_tools.rs`: `add_sketch_recipe`, `edit_sketch_recipe` and `add_quick_op`. `get_job` profiles show `recipe`.\n- `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md` is generated again. The guide table names the three tools.\n- The decision record is `docs/decisions/3194-sketch-recipes.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nUsers who cut simple shapes without a CAD model had no way to state a shape by its dimensions.\n\n## Tests\n\nPinning tests:\n\n- `camcraft-geometry` `dxf` suite, module `sketch_recipe` (9 tests): each shape is one closed chain with the exact perimeter and bounds; bad dimensions are refused by name; the same recipe gives the same outline bit for bit.\n- `camcraft-app` `mcp` suite, module `sketch_recipe` (5 tests):\n  - `each_quick_op_shape_generates_verifies_and_posts_with_no_model`: four shapes, generate, `verify` ok, Fanuc post, lowest feed Z is the stated depth, G2/G3 for the round shapes.\n  - `a_quick_op_undoes_and_redoes_in_one_step`.\n  - `a_refused_quick_op_places_nothing_and_leaves_no_history`.\n  - `editing_a_recipe_regenerates_the_outline_and_stales_its_operation`.\n  - `a_recipe_profile_round_trips_the_project_file_and_edits_after_load` (v85 written, recipe and placement read back, a changed recipe refused as corrupt).\n- `mcp_doc_drift`: 9 passed.\n\nRed before the change: the pins do not compile on the base (`unresolved import camcraft_geometry::sketch_recipe`).\n\nMutation checks (each guard removed, pin run, guard restored):\n\n| Guard | Pin | Without guard | Restored |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| corner radius above half the smaller side | `bad_dimensions_are_refused_by_name_and_never_clamped` | red (the bad rectangle compiled) | green |\n| recipe must give the stored outline on load | `a_recipe_profile_round_trips_...` | red | green |\n| quick op removes its trial profile | `a_refused_quick_op_places_nothing_...` | red | green |\n| only a recipe profile takes an edit | `editing_a_recipe_regenerates_...` | red | green |\n\nGate on the final head:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base d5544b6f5` (the branch base): 1015 steps, 1014 ok. The one red step was `app suites: continuous_4axis_part`: `the_committed_project_uses_the_current_file_version` asks for the new file version. This PR steps `examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.camproj` from `\"version\": 84` to `85` (only that line, as b376f74fa did for v84). The committed program does not change. The step was run again with `--failed`: 1 step, ok. The quick plan includes the `example_catalog*` suites: all ok.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-geometry -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\n- `examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.camproj`: only the line `\"version\": 84` becomes `85` (the file version step). Its program `.nc` does not change.\n- No other `*.nc`, `*.cl` or `examples/catalog/**` file changed. The diff changes no generator or post. The quick plan ran the `example_catalog*` suites: all ok.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The compact UI form on the Stock page. This PR has no UI change. The form is filed as #4464 (P7). The text profile of #2679 also has no UI form.\n- No script verbs. The MCP tools call the commands directly, as `move_dxf_profile` does.\n- No row in `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md` (a process file). The generated reference lists the tools.\n- Heavy lanes: not run. AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\" (#3556) gives no heavy step to a P6 PR. The diff changes no toolpath generator, simulation or post.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nThese open PRs touch the same files, in different functions (tool registry lists and the schema). Whichever merges second refreshes:\n\n- #4438, #4302, #4238: `crates/app/src/mcp/mod.rs` and `tools.rs` (module and registry lines).\n- #4288: `crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs`, `crates/app/src/project/mod.rs`.\n- #4066: `crates/app/src/schema.rs`.\n\nThis PR steps `PROJECT_VERSION` to 85. Another PR that steps it too must take the next number.\n\nNew top-level test files: none. The tests join the `dxf` suite (geometry) and the `mcp` suite (app).\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Quick ops - place a rectangle, circle, obround or polygon by its dimensions as a stock profile, with a 2D Contour on it in one undo step; edit the dimensions in place (MCP `add_sketch_recipe`, `edit_sketch_recipe`, `add_quick_op`). Project files are now v85.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: project files are v85; a v84 reader refuses them.\n\nFixes #3194\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
